    {
      "id": "new-transparency",
      "file": "main",
      "text": "The history-coordinate comparison is a post hoc discovery on an existing simulation grid. We recorded the subsequent simulation equations, random streams, classification criteria and financial crossing predictions before running their new calculations, with local design commits and chronology available in the repository. This is a pre-run specification within an already examined research program, not a public external registration or an untouched financial holdout. The new simulations change innovation laws and random streams, whereas the FX learning curve reuses the known validation and evaluation period.\n\nEvery history shares the original validation segment and evaluation start, with complete mature-label pools and the original update convention; unavailable cases would remain NA. Both W2880 cases exactly reproduced all available old scientific arrays, summary fields and parameter selections before other histories were attempted. Some older parsimonious trace fields were absent, so their unavailable historical comparisons remain outside that claim. The bootstrap holds the selected coordinate fixed when resampling repetition clusters; its endpoint envelope conditions on that choice and the discovery grid. The new paired-loss diagnostics use the original Bartlett HAC convention with a normal reference and no family adjustment, treating financial dependence conditions as working premises.",
      "bindings": [
        {
          "kind": "digit",
          "offset": 800,
          "literal": "2880",
          "source": "protocol/revision-v9/wp3-learning-curve.json",
          "source_sha256": "0490302463c17096b612fa7241cae97fed082052cefd29f176f0eba3926aedae",
          "pointer": "/run_order/0/1",
