    {
      "id": "discovery-coordinate-and-cutpoints",
      "file": "main",
      "text": "The post hoc selected coordinate is \\(c=W/(H+1)\\), a history-to-horizon proxy that omits coefficient count and differs from estimated effective sample size. On the discovery grid, the original regression's first cutpoint is 106.5, whereas the smaller regression's first cutpoint is 27.32. Both wide endpoint envelopes condition on the selected coordinate and grid, omit selection adjustment and allow multiple crossings for the smaller regression. These descriptions motivate a test of history sensitivity under changed innovation laws and additional histories.",
