    {
      "id": "unified-caption",
      "file": "main",
      "text": "\\caption{Conditional-regression loss against same-history historical headroom on a logarithmic \\(c=W/(H+1)\\) axis; this coordinate excludes coefficient count. Light marks distinguish discovery and confirmation simulations; dark marks distinguish financial tasks, with lower panels repeating a labelled detail range. Discovery bands and dashed lines show post hoc first-cutpoint envelopes and point estimates from raw-coordinate interpolation across pooled horizons. Financial crossings interpolate raw history within each horizon on the reused FX period: three agree with prespecified intervals, while the remaining case stays untestable through left censoring. Both longer-horizon curves lose again at the largest history, and the universal simplification criterion fails in the confirmation experiment. Consistency supports a partial history pattern; horizon collapse and coefficient normalization remain unidentified.}\\label{fig:mechanism}",
